!default.xcworkspace

# ── Firebase (generated) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bookly does NOT apply the `com.google.gms.google-services` Gradle plugin
# and does not ship `google-services.json`: the flavors are two application
# ids, so the flavor → appId mapping is held in typed Dart instead, at
# `lib/core/config/firebase_options.dart`. That file is source, not a build
# artifact — a fresh clone needs it to compile, so it is committed.
#
# The rules below keep the FlutterFire CLI's default outputs ignored. If a
# future `flutterfire configure` runs with its default `--out`, it writes a
# single-configuration `lib/firebase_options.dart` that would silently
# shadow the merged one, and re-injects the Gradle plugin plus
# `google-services.json`. None of the three should reach a commit; revert
# the Gradle edit by hand when it happens.
#
# None of this is about confidentiality: the API key is public, ships in the
# app bundle, and is guarded by package name + SHA. It is about diffs and
# keeping one source of truth.
lib/firebase_options.dart
android/app/google-services.json
firebase.json

# ── Supabase local ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# ── Executing-plans scratch workspace (git-ignored by design) ────────
.superpowers/

# ── Logs / scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
